    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Qing was a Manchu dynasty that conquered Ming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a> in 1644 and ruled the world's most populous empire.</li><li>It reached its greatest extent in the 18th century, setting the territorial framework of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a>.</li><li>Rebellion, defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#opium-wars">Opium Wars</a> and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#japan">Japan</a>, and failed reform led to revolution and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#puyi">Puyi</a>'s abdication in 1912.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#nurhaci">Nurhaci</a>'s Banner system organised the entire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#jurchens">Jurchen</a> population into colour-coded units that were at once army formations, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#census">census</a> registers and social structures.</p></aside>
    </section>

